## Findings

| Severity | Location | Concrete failure and fix |
|---|---|---|
| **BLOCKER** | [SafeDeleter.swift:126](/Users/sandy/Projects/SystemDataLens/Shared/SafeDeleter.swift:126) | After walking a directory through `cfd`, the code closes it and removes the *name*. Another process can replace that name with a different empty directory before `unlinkat`, causing deletion outside the inspected tree. The file branch at line 133 has the same identity race and can remove a replacement file, including one with a different owner. Recheck name, device, inode, type, and owner immediately before removal; because a recheck alone still races, use a design that can establish exclusive control over the entry before unlinking, or fail closed where that cannot be guaranteed. |
| **BLOCKER** | [BulkScanner.swift:211](/Users/sandy/Projects/SystemDataLens/Shared/BulkScanner.swift:211) | `ATTR_CMN_ERROR` is parsed before name, device, type, flags, and file ID, despite its later bitmap position. Entries reporting an error shift every subsequent read; names, sizes, and directory decisions can become corrupt. Parse common attributes in bitmap order, with bounds checks against each record’s length. |
| **BLOCKER** | [BulkScanner.swift:143](/Users/sandy/Projects/SystemDataLens/Shared/BulkScanner.swift:143) | Record length and name offset/length are trusted without checking they remain inside the 256 KiB buffer or the current record. A malformed or unexpected kernel record can cause out-of-bounds reads or an invalid cursor. Validate each record before parsing or advancing. |
| **SHOULD** | [HelperSession.swift:219](/Users/sandy/Projects/SystemDataLens/Helper/HelperSession.swift:219) | Helper verification uses `.extendRights`; that requests or extends the admin right instead of solely checking the right supplied by the app. Verify the existing right without extension or interaction, and reject when it is absent. |
| **SHOULD** | [HelperSession.swift:195](/Users/sandy/Projects/SystemDataLens/Helper/HelperSession.swift:195) | Any accepted client can make the root helper exit, including during another connection’s scan or cleanup. Restrict upgrade exit to an idle helper and a verified version transition. |
| **SHOULD** | [BulkScanner.swift:132](/Users/sandy/Projects/SystemDataLens/Shared/BulkScanner.swift:132) | Directories are reopened later by absolute path without comparing their identity to the entry that was scanned. A renamed or replaced directory can redirect the scan, including into another device. Carry directory descriptors or verify `fstat` against the recorded identity before reading. |
| **SHOULD** | [FlatTree.swift:257](/Users/sandy/Projects/SystemDataLens/Shared/FlatTree.swift:257) | Decode arithmetic such as `n * size` and `off + blobLen` can overflow before the bounds check. Use checked subtraction/division against remaining bytes before allocating arrays. |
| **SHOULD** | [HelperSession.swift:91](/Users/sandy/Projects/SystemDataLens/Helper/HelperSession.swift:91), [HelperClient.swift:186](/Users/sandy/Projects/SystemDataLens/App/Services/HelperClient.swift:186) | A large scan exists simultaneously as a tree, encoded blob, 8 MiB chunk copies, assembled app blob, and decoded app tree. Multi-million-node scans can exhaust memory in both processes. Stream encoding and transfer with bounded storage, or enforce a measured size limit and report it before allocation. |
| **SHOULD** | [Categories.swift:146](/Users/sandy/Projects/SystemDataLens/App/Model/Categories.swift:146) | `states` stores a dictionary entry and array for every matched node. Broad home rules can match millions of nodes, adding substantial avoidable memory to an already large tree. Store compact per-node trie state or discard parent state once its children are classified. |
| **SHOULD** | [UserCleanup.swift:59](/Users/sandy/Projects/SystemDataLens/App/Services/UserCleanup.swift:59) | DriveFS account names are used as path components without `isSafeName`; a `..` entry cannot come from a normal directory listing, but symlinks and account-directory changes between listing and deletion make the preview and executed target diverge. Validate names and bind each selected target to the exact previewed entries before running. |
| **SHOULD** | [InspectorView.swift:140](/Users/sandy/Projects/SystemDataLens/App/Views/InspectorView.swift:140) | “Move to Trash” acts on a path from an earlier scan with no identity check. If that path now names a different item, the app trashes the replacement. Record and compare device/inode at confirmation, then resolve the action against that same item or require a fresh scan. |
| **SHOULD** | [CleanupView.swift:44](/Users/sandy/Projects/SystemDataLens/App/Views/CleanupView.swift:44) | User cleanup runs before root authorization. If authorization is cancelled, the operation is already partly destructive despite the combined confirmation. Obtain root authorization before executing any selected target, then report per-target completion. |
| **NIT** | [HelperClient.swift:142](/Users/sandy/Projects/SystemDataLens/App/Services/HelperClient.swift:142) | `OnceFlag` prevents double resume, but a connection that neither replies nor invokes its error handler leaves the continuation suspended forever. Add a timeout and invalidate that connection when it expires. |

This was a source review only; I did not edit files or run destructive checks.
